 appropriate for a forensic investigation task.\"\n    },\n    \"task_readme\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n        \"explanation\": \"environment/README.md provides helpful dev/build context regarding disk.tar.gz and sas-mock without duplicating instruction content.\"\n    },\n    \"expert_time_estimate\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The expert_time_esti"]
[196.6724, "i", "mate_hours metadata field is omitted from task.toml.\"\n    },\n    \"task_toml_schema\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n        \"explanation\": \"task.toml uses non-standard metadata field \\\"difficulty\\\" while omitting required benchmark metadata fields (difficulty_explanation, solution_explanation, verification_explanation, subcategory, expert_time_estimate_hours).\"\n    },\n    \"no_extraneous_files\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The task directory contains unused extraneous baseline reports under baselines/ (alert-transcriber, noop, oracle) and unused files under assets/ that are not referenced by Dockerfiles, instructions, solution, or tests.\"\n    },\n    \"artifact_efficiency\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"not_applicable\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The deliverables are inherently small text markdown files produced by the agent.\"\n    },\n    \"verifier_execution_isolation\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"not_applicable\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The verifier parses text/markdown files and never executes agent-produced code or scripts.\"\n    },\n    \"ctrf_reporting\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"fail\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The verifier does not output CTRF test results to /logs/verifier/ctrf.json.\"\n    },\n    \"do_not_modify_enforced\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n        \"explanation\": \"The instruction specifies that /disk is read-only, which is enforced via filesystem read-only permissions in the container setup.\"\n    },\n    \"binary_reward\": {\n        \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n        \"explanation\": \"tests/test.sh writes either 1.0 or 0.0 to /logs/verifier/reward.txt.\"\n    }\n}\n\nwith open(\"check-result.json\", \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n\nprint(\"Done\")\n'\n"]
